{# Reader-facing disclaimer, rendered at the top of every generated DisMech page.

   Always present until the reader dismisses it: someone who lands on a single
   disorder page from a search engine or an external link never sees the project
   documentation, so the AI-curated provenance of the content and its
   unsuitability for clinical use have to travel with the page itself.

   Dismissal lasts for the browsing session only, via the sessionStorage key
   `dismech-disclaimer-dismissed` (issue #7421). sessionStorage is scoped to one
   tab and cleared when it closes, so moving between DisMech pages in the same
   tab keeps the bar dismissed, while a fresh tab or a later visit shows it
   again. Deliberately NOT localStorage: the statement should come back, not be
   silenced permanently.

   The dismiss button is CSS-hidden by default and revealed by the script below,
   so a reader without JavaScript is never shown a control that cannot work.

   Because the bar can be dismissed, generated disorder and module pages also
   carry the non-dismissible one-line `_disclaimer_footer.html.j2` in their page
   footer, so the statement never disappears from the page entirely.

   The disclaimer URL is deliberately ABSOLUTE, not relative. Pages using this
   partial live at varying depths (pages/disorders/X.html, pages/modules/X.html,
   …) and the canonical text is published by MkDocs under /elements/, which is a
   separate build from these pages — so there is no relative path that is correct
   everywhere. Please do not "fix" this into a relative link. The trade-off is
   that a local preview links out to the production copy.

   Rationale: docs/explanation/design-decisions.md (§11).
   Canonical long-form text: docs/disclaimer.md.
   Keep the wording here, in docs/disclaimer.md, and in the inlined copies on the
   hand-maintained site pages (index.html, app/, details/) in step. #}
<aside class="dismech-disclaimer" aria-label="DisMech disclaimer">
    <p>
        <strong>AI-curated research resource &mdash; not medical advice.</strong>
        DisMech content is generated and maintained by AI curation agents under human
        review, from publicly accessible literature and curated biomedical knowledge
        resources. Nothing here is intended to inform medical diagnosis or treatment.
        <a href="https://dismech.monarchinitiative.org/elements/disclaimer/">Read the full disclaimer</a>.
    </p>
    <button type="button" class="dismech-disclaimer-dismiss"
            aria-label="Dismiss this disclaimer" title="Dismiss this disclaimer">
        <span aria-hidden="true">&times;</span>
    </button>
</aside>
{# Runs synchronously, immediately after the bar, so an already-dismissed bar is
   hidden before first paint rather than flashing and disappearing. #}
<script>
    (function () {
        var KEY = 'dismech-disclaimer-dismissed';
        var bar = document.querySelector('.dismech-disclaimer');
        if (!bar) { return; }
        // sessionStorage access itself throws when storage is blocked (Safari
        // private browsing, cookies-disabled), so every use is guarded.
        var store = null;
        try { store = window.sessionStorage; } catch (err) { store = null; }
        try {
            if (store && store.getItem(KEY) === '1') { bar.hidden = true; return; }
        } catch (err) { /* unreadable storage: show the bar */ }
        var button = bar.querySelector('.dismech-disclaimer-dismiss');
        if (!button) { return; }
        bar.classList.add('is-dismissible');
        button.addEventListener('click', function () {
            bar.hidden = true;
            try { if (store) { store.setItem(KEY, '1'); } } catch (err) { /* not persisted */ }
            // Focus would otherwise fall back to <body>, losing a keyboard
            // reader's place. preventScroll keeps the viewport where it was.
            var next = document.querySelector('main, h1');
            if (next) {
                if (!next.hasAttribute('tabindex')) { next.setAttribute('tabindex', '-1'); }
                try { next.focus({ preventScroll: true }); } catch (err) { next.focus(); }
            }
        });
    })();
</script>
